note omtex feature tour: Omega listings checked by the pinned compiler, math, a table, a figure, citations.
note Build: tools/build.sh examples/listings/paper.om   (the listing check runs as part of the build)
text cls "article"
text clso "11pt"
text pfont "fontenc"
text pfonto "T1"
text pgeo "geometry"
text pgeoo "margin=1in"
text pams "amsmath"
text pgfx "graphicx"
text phyp "hyperref"
text phypo "hidelinks"
text ttl "Writing papers in Omega with omtex"
text who "omtex examples"
text when "October 2026"
text abs "This paper is an Omega program. Every byte of its LaTeX was written by checked Omega code, every special character was escaped or refused, and every Omega listing below was compiled by the pinned seeded compiler while the paper was built."
text s1 "Listings that must compile"
text l1 "sec:listings"
text p1 "An `omlisting` is compiled with the pinned `omc` when the paper is built with `check`. Listing[#lst:add3] must compile; the build fails otherwise."
text c1 "Adding three"
text k1 "lst:add3"
text b1 "note add three to a number\nfn add3 x ulong to ulong\nret add x 3\nend\nfn main to int\nret int sub add3 4 7\nend\n"
text p2 "A listing can also state that the compiler must *refuse* it, and with which error. Listing[#lst:dead] has a statement after `ret`, which is error 17."
text c2 "Refused: a line after `ret` (error 17)"
text k2 "lst:dead"
text b2 "fn main to int\nret 0\nret 1\nend\n"
text p3 "A fragment is shown but explicitly not compiled; the check reports it as NOT_CHECKED."
text c3 "A fragment"
text k3 "lst:frag"
text b3 "i = add i 1\n"
text p4 "Other languages use `codelang` and `listing`:"
text sh "sh"
text c4 "Building this paper"
text k4 "lst:build"
text b4 "tools/build.sh examples/listings/paper.om\n"
text s2 "Mathematics"
text l2 "sec:math"
text l3 "sec:more"
text p5 "Inline math such as $e^{i\\pi} + 1 = 0$ is checked: braces must balance, and $\\%$, $\\$$ and $\\#$ only appear escaped. Display math:"
text m1 "\\int_0^1 x^2 \\, dx = \\frac{1}{3}"
text k5 "eq:int"
text p6 "Equation[#eq:int] was checked with Wolfram Language (`Integrate[x^2,{x,0,1}]` gives 1/3). An aligned pair:"
text m2 "(a+b)^2 &= a^2 + 2ab + b^2 \\\\\n(a-b)^2 &= a^2 - 2ab + b^2"
text s3 "Tables, figures and citations"
text p7 "Table[#tab:esc] lists what prose characters become. Figure[#fig:ex] is a stock image. Information theory begins with Shannon[@shannon48]; the listing style follows the `listings` manual[@listings]."
text tc "Prose characters and their LaTeX"
text tk "tab:esc"
text ts "ll"
text h1 "Prose"
text h2 "LaTeX"
text r1a "`50% & 3_x #1 {a}`"
text r1b "`50\\% \\& 3\\_x \\#1 \\{a\\}`"
text r2a "`*word*` and `**word**`"
text r2b "`\\emph{word}` and `\\textbf{word}`"
text r3a "`[@key]` and `[#label]`"
text r3b "`~\\cite{key}` and `~\\ref{label}`"
text fp "example-image"
text fc "A stock image from the `mwe` package."
text fk "fig:ex"
text e1 "shannon48"
text e1t "C. E. Shannon. A mathematical theory of communication. *Bell System Technical Journal*, 27(3):379--423, 1948."
text e2 "listings"
text e2t "C. Heinz, B. Moses and J. Hoffmann. *The Listings Package*. CTAN, 2024."
fn main to int
docclass clso cls
usepkgo pfonto pfont
usepkgo pgeoo pgeo
usepkg pams
usepkg pgfx
usepkgo phypo phyp
omlang
title ttl
author who
date when
begindoc
maketitle
docabstract abs
sectionl s1 l1
para p1
omlisting c1 k1 b1
para p2
omrefuse 17
omlisting c2 k2 b2
para p3
omfragment c3 k3 b3
para p4
codelang sh
listing c4 k4 b4
sectionl s2 l2
prose p5
equationl k5 m1
parbreak
prose p6
align m2
sectionl s3 l3
para p7
table tc tk ts
hline
cell h1
cell h2
row
hline
cell r1a
cell r1b
row
cell r2a
cell r2b
row
cell r3a
cell r3b
row
hline
endtable
figure fp fc fk
bibbegin
bibitem e1 e1t
bibitem e2 e2t
endlist
enddoc
ret 0
end
